# Task Assignment Rules

## TaskAssignmentRule
- rule_type: `workflow_stage` | `issue_category` | `review_status`
- match_value: varies by type
  - workflow_stage: FUNDS, RECOS, NOTIFY, EXEC, UPDATE, COMPLETED
  - issue_category: PORTFOLIO_PERFORMANCE, RECOMMENDATION_MATCH, CASHFLOW, etc.
  - review_status: initiated, sent, meeting, closed

## Service Functions
- `get_assignee_for_workflow_stage(workflow)` – monthly investment workflows
- `get_assignee_for_issue(issue)` – DataIntegrityIssue
- `get_assignee_for_review_status(workflow)` – ReviewWorkflow
- `apply_review_assignment(workflow)` – sets assigned_to (OpsTask create gated off by default)
- `create_ops_task_from_issue(issue)` – DataIntegrityIssue → OpsTask (`DI_CREATE_OPS_TASKS`, default false)
- `create_ops_task_from_review_workflow(workflow)` – ReviewWorkflow → OpsTask (`REVIEW_CREATE_OPS_TASKS`, default false)

## OpsTask Links
- `data_integrity_issue_id` – when created from DataIntegrityIssue
- `review_workflow_id` – when created from ReviewWorkflow
- Auto-create is **off by default**. Users may create tasks for their own tracking.
- Backlog cleanup: `scripts/retire_auto_created_ops_tasks.py` (see `docs/PROD_DATA_CLEANUP_SCRIPTS.md`)

## Admin
- UI: `/admin/task-assignment-rules`
- Blueprint: `routes/task_assignment_rules.py`
- Seed: `python migrations/seed_task_assignment_rules.py`
